# CMT input path as the ROM's LOAD routine programs it: the cassette
# line feeds CA1 (falling edge, PCR0=0) and CB1 (rising edge, PCR4=1),
# T2 measures the interval between edges, IER=$92 enables both.
# Edge pairs simulate 2400Hz half-cycles (186) and 1200Hz (373, longer
# than T2=$0107=263 so the T2 timeout flag separates the two tones).
N 1800
W 5 B 00
W 10 C FE
W 15 E 92
W 20 8 07
W 25 9 01
# leader-ish 2400Hz half-cycles
E 100 A 1
E 100 B 1
W 104 D FF
E 286 A 0
E 286 B 0
W 290 D FF
W 294 9 01
E 472 A 1
E 472 B 1
W 476 D FF
W 480 9 01
# 1200Hz half-cycle: T2 ($0107) times out before the next edge
E 845 A 0
E 845 B 0
R 849 8
W 853 D FF
W 857 9 01
E 1218 A 1
E 1218 B 1
W 1222 D FF
W 1226 9 01
# back to 2400Hz
E 1404 A 0
E 1404 B 0
W 1408 D FF
W 1412 9 01
E 1590 A 1
E 1590 B 1
W 1594 D FF
